{"content":[{"c":["HEMORRHAGE"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Issue of blood, coming from any cut or nosebleed (",{"href":"?bref=Pr.30.33","r":"Pr.30.33","rawR":"Pr.30.33","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Pr.30.33","value":"Pr.30.33"}],"t":"ref","v":"Prv 30:33"},"). However, in Scripture it almost always refers to vaginal bleeding. Laws concerning normal and abnormal menstruation are given in ",{"href":"?bref=Lev.15.19-30","r":"Lev.15.19-30","rawR":"Lev.15.19-30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.15.19-30","value":"Lev.15.19-30"}],"t":"ref","v":"Leviticus 15:19-30"},". A woman with normal menstruation was considered unclean for seven days, along with anything that came into contact with her. A woman who bled longer than seven days was unclean as long as she was bleeding plus seven additional days."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["All the Gospels except John give an account of the miraculous healing by Jesus of the woman who had a hemorrhage for 12 years (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.9.20-22","r":"Matt.9.20-22","rawR":"Matt.9.20-22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.9.20-22","value":"Matt.9.20-22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 9:20-22"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.5.25-34","r":"Mark.5.25-34","rawR":"Mark.5.25-34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.5.25-34","value":"Mark.5.25-34"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mk 5:25-34"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.8.43-48","r":"Luke.8.43-48","rawR":"Luke.8.43-48","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.8.43-48","value":"Luke.8.43-48"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 8:43-48"},"). By touching Jesus’ garment, the woman was actually violating the OT laws concerning menstruation and making Jesus’ garment unclean (",{"href":"?bref=Lev.15.1-33","r":"Lev.15.1-33","rawR":"Lev.15.1-33","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.15.1-33","value":"Lev.15.1-33"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lv 15"},"). Her courageous act of faith in Jesus healed her."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=MedicineandMedicalPractice_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"MedicineandMedicalPractice_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"MedicineandMedicalPractice_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Medicine and Medical Practice"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Hemorrhage","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Prv 30:33","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Pr.30.33","rawQueryValue":"Pr.30.33","sourceRefExact":"Pr.30.33"},{"anchorText":"Leviticus 15:19-30","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Lev.15.19-30","rawQueryValue":"Lev.15.19-30","sourceRefExact":"Lev.15.19-30"},{"anchorText":"Mt 9:20-22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Matt.9.20-22","rawQueryValue":"Matt.9.20-22","sourceRefExact":"Matt.9.20-22"},{"anchorText":"Mk 5:25-34","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Mark.5.25-34","rawQueryValue":"Mark.5.25-34","sourceRefExact":"Mark.5.25-34"},{"anchorText":"Lk 8:43-48","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Luke.8.43-48","rawQueryValue":"Luke.8.43-48","sourceRefExact":"Luke.8.43-48"},{"anchorText":"Lv 15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Lev.15.1-33","rawQueryValue":"Lev.15.1-33","sourceRefExact":"Lev.15.1-33"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"712a497dc7906cf9009d60852c77d152f2371912d17f88c038ed181ea3814dc6","sourceItemName":"Hemorrhage","sourceItemOrder":244,"sourceMember":"Articles/H.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Hemorrhage","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Hemorrhage","title":"Hemorrhage","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}